# UTC. work 5m, from contracts/entrypoints.md §스케줄. Cron and not a resident daemon because
# `collectors/youtube/cli.py:_run_work` is a batch: it claims up to DEFAULT_WORK_BATCH (50) queued
# jobs, works them, and returns -- there is no poll loop and no --poll flag to give it one, so the
# repetition has to come from outside the process. (The archived tubedepth worker was a daemon with
# `work --poll 5`; that flag did not come across into this CLI.)
#
# 5 minutes drains faster than watch fills: 50 jobs a pass is 600 an hour against one watch sweep an
# hour, so a backlog shrinks between sweeps instead of growing. Overlap is safe by construction -- if
# one pass is still running when the next fires, `_claim`'s single `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` statement
# means the second cannot see the first's rows as queued.
#
# The only youtube line that spends an external request budget, which is why it is alone here.
#
# Phase 2, not 0: a 5-minute line cannot dodge every commerce window and does not need to (different
# hosts, different schema, a bounded 50-job batch). Offsetting it by two minutes only keeps it off the
# minutes the rest of the stack already starts on -- :00 every hour (ranking), 05:00 (analyze all),
# and the quarter hours collector-youtube-flatten used to sit on.
2-59/5 * * * *   cosmai collect youtube --dataset work
